 World stork that is glossy black above and white below\"],[0,11,829272,2157,\"n:02024449-n | seabird | a bird that frequents coastal waters and the open ocean: gulls, pelicans, gannets, cormorants, albatrosses, petrels, etc.\"],[0,11,829809,2158,\"n:02025338-n | shore bird | any of numerous wading birds that frequent mostly seashores and estuaries\"],[0,11,830268,2159,\"n:02035423-n | half snipe | a small short-billed Old World snipe\"],[0,11,830658,2160,\"n:02051742-n | diver | large somewhat primitive fish-eating diving bird of the Northern Hemisphere having webbed feet placed far back\"],[0,11,831158,2161,\"n:02059382-n | emperor penguin | the largest penguin\"],[0,11,831515,2162,\"n:02060385-n | pelagic bird | bird of the open seas\"],[0,11,831860,2163,\"n:02074692-n | river dolphin | any of several long-snouted usually freshwater dolphins of South America and southern Asia\"],[0,11,832328,2164,\"n:02084223-n | sea horse | either of two large northern marine mammals having ivory tusks and tough hide over thick blubber\"],[0,11,832818,2165,\"n:02087513-n | cur | an inferior dog or one of mixed breed\"],[0,11,833169,2166,\"n:02089774-n | hunting dog | a dog used in hunting game\"],[0,11,833503,2167,\"n:02091118-n | bloodhound | a breed of large powerful hound of European origin having very acute smell and used in tracking\"],[0,11,833995,2168,\"n:02092120-n | sausage dog | informal term\"],[0,11,834321,2169,\"n:02096643-n | irish terrier | medium-sized breed with a wiry brown coat\"],[0,11,834692,2170,\"n:02098379-n | welsh terrier | wire-haired terrier resembling Airedales but smaller\"],[0,11,835085,2171,\"n:02099950-n | scotch terrier | old Scottish breed of small long-haired usually black terrier with erect tail and ears\"],[0,11,835583,2172,\"n:02100126-n | chrysanthemum dog | breed of medium-sized terriers bred in Tibet resembling Old English sheepdogs with fluffy curled tails\"],[0,11,836107,2173,\"n:02101458-n | bird dog | a gun dog trained to locate or r