 the process of remembering (especially the process of recovering information by mental effort)\"],[0,11,1937980,4930,\"n:05769915-n | anamnesis | the ability to recall past occurrences\"],[0,11,1938363,4931,\"n:05770995-n | identification | the process of recognizing something or someone by remembering\"],[0,11,1938792,4932,\"n:05771409-n | identity | the individual characteristics by which a thing or person is recognized or known\"],[0,11,1939223,4933,\"n:05771913-n | association | the process of bringing ideas or events together in memory or imagination\"],[0,11,1939687,4934,\"n:05773412-n | symbol | something visible that by association or convention represents something else that is invisible\"],[0,11,1940206,4935,\"n:05775730-n | imagery | the ability to form mental images of things or events\"],[0,11,1940627,4936,\"n:05776104-n | mind's eye | the imaging of remembered or invented scenes\"],[0,11,1940992,4937,\"n:05776249-n | vision | a vivid mental image\"],[0,11,1941297,4938,\"n:05776803-n | dream | imaginative thoughts indulged in while awake\"],[0,11,1941660,4939,\"n:05777059-n | nightmare | a terrifying or deeply upsetting dream\"],[0,11,1942019,4940,\"n:05777830-n | evocation | imaginative re-creation\"],[0,11,1942339,4941,\"n:05778923-n | cerebration | the process of using your mind to consider something carefully\"],[0,11,1942819,4942,\"n:05779833-n | construction | the creation of a construct\"],[0,11,1943177,4943,\"n:05780353-n | abstract thought | thinking that is coherent and logical\"],[0,11,1943581,4944,\"n:05780664-n | analysis | the abstract separation of a whole into its constituent parts in order to study the parts and their relations\"],[0,11,1944092,4945,\"n:05781046-n | argument | a course of reasoning aimed at demonstrating a truth or falsehood\"],[0,11,1944563,4946,\"n:05782126-n | deduction | reasoning from the general to the particular (or from cause to effect)\"],[0,11,1945015,4947,\"n:05782412-n | generalisation | reasoning from deta