 the branch of military science dealing with detailed maneuvers to achieve objectives set by strategy\"],[0,11,2114896,5361,\"n:06261911-n | transmission | communication by means of transmitted signals\"],[0,11,2115269,5362,\"n:06262268-n | communicating | the activity of communicating\"],[0,11,2115631,5363,\"n:06263270-n | airing | the opening of a subject to widespread discussion and debate\"],[0,11,2116068,5364,\"n:06263648-n | extension | the spreading of something (a belief or practice) into new regions\"],[0,11,2116490,5365,\"n:06263820-n | message | a communication (usually brief) that is written or spoken or signaled\"],[0,11,2116896,5366,\"n:06264137-n | broadcast | message that is transmitted by radio or television\"],[0,11,2117270,5367,\"n:06264369-n | cipher | a message written in a secret code\"],[0,11,2117614,5368,\"n:06264605-n | medium | an intervening substance through which signals can travel as a means for communication\"],[0,11,2118051,5369,\"n:06265081-n | cold medium | a medium that usually, but not always, provides little involvement together with substantial stimulus\"],[0,11,2118551,5370,\"n:06265658-n | vehicle | a medium for the expression or achievement of something\"],[0,11,2118929,5371,\"n:06266354-n | piece of paper | paper used for writing or printing\"],[0,11,2119315,5372,\"n:06267949-n | half page | something that covers (the top or bottom) half of a page\"],[0,11,2119703,5373,\"n:06268230-n | title page | a page of a book displaying the title and author and publisher\"],[0,11,2120104,5374,\"n:06269680-n | letterhead | a sheet of stationery with name and address of the organization printed at the top\"],[0,11,2120546,5375,\"n:06270389-n | worksheet | a sheet of paper with multiple columns\"],[0,11,2120896,5376,\"n:06270774-n | channel | (often plural) a means of communication or access\"],[0,11,2121297,5377,\"n:06271913-n | contact | a channel for communication between groups\"],[0,11,2121700,5378,\"n:06273220-n | celluloid | a medium that disseminates moving pictures\"],[0,11,2122079,5379,\"n:06274548-n | magnetic medium | any storage medium in which different patterns of magnetization are used to represent stored bits or bytes of information\"],[0,11,2122664,5380,\"n:06274829-n | broadcast medium | a medium that disseminates via telecommunications\"],[0,11,2123074,5381,\"n:06277070-n | journalism | newspapers and magazines collectively\"],[0,11,2123440,5382,\"n:06278411-n | school newspaper | a newspaper written and published by students in a school\"],[0,11,2123868,5383,\"n:06278411-n | school paper | a newspaper written and published by students in a school\"],[0,11,2124288,5384,\"n:06278749-n | article | nonfictional prose forming an independent part of a publication\"],[0,11,2124682,5385,\"n:06279220-n | column | an article giving opinions or perspectives\"],[0,11,2125066,5386,\"n:06280049-n | piece | an artistic or literary composition\"],[0,11,2125398,5387,\"n:06280609-n | paper | a scholarly article describing the results of observations or stating hypotheses\"],[0,11,2125820,5388,\"n:06280961-n | reissue | a publication (such as a book) that is reprinted without changes or editing and offered again for sale\"],[0,11,2126319,5389,\"n:06281194-n | new edition | a publication (such as a book) that has been modified or updated and offered again for sale\"],[0,11,2126781,5390,\"n:06281708-n | opening line | the first line of a piece of writing (as a newspaper story)\"],[0,11,2127184,5391,\"n:06283456-n | call | a method of contacting a person by phone\"],[0,11,2127557,5392,\"n:06283860-n | call back | a return call\"],[0,11,2127857,5393,\"n:06284543-n | crank call | a hostile telephone call (from a crank)\"],[0,11,2128212,5394,\"n:06284639-n | local call | a telephone call made within a local calling area\"],[0,11,2128587,5395,\"n:06285748-n | cable | a telegram sent abroad\"],[0,11,2128930,5396,\"n:06286287-n | mail | the bags of letters and packages that are transported by the postal service\"],[0,11,2129339,5397,\"n:06288456-n | picture | the visible part of a television transmission\"],[0,11,2129707,5398,\"n:06291693-n | reception | quality or fidelity of a received broadcast\"],[0,11,2130067,5399,\"n:06291948-n | modulation | (electronics) the transmission of a signal by using it to vary a carrier wave\"],[0,11,2130498,5400,\"n:06294417-n | words | language that is spoken or written\"],[0,11,2130828,5401,\"n:06294720-n | object language | the language into which a text written in another language is to be translated\"],[0,11,2131296,5402,\"n:06294878-n | language unit | one of the natural units into which linguistic messages can be analyzed\"],[0,11,2131754,5403,\"n:06295551-n | context | discourse that surrounds a language unit and helps to determine its interpretation\"],[0,11,2132228,5404,\"n:06298695-n | antonym | a word that expresses a meaning opposed to the meaning of another word, in which case the two words are antonyms of each other\"],[0,11,2132779,5405,\"n:06299307-n | portmanteau word | a new word formed by joining two others and combining their meanings\"],[0,11,2133239,5406,\"n:06310906-n | singular form | the form of a word that is used to denote a singleton\"],[0,11,2133646,5407,\"n:06311813-n | dictionary entry | the entry in a dictionary of information about a word\"],[0,11,2134065,5408,\"n:06313073-n | polysyllabic word | a word of more than three syllables\"],[0,11,2134453,5409,\"n:06314672-n | equivalent word | two words that can be interchanged in a context are said to be synonymous relative to that context\"],[0,11,2134953,5410,\"n:06314878-n | term | a word or expression used for some particular thing\"],[0,11,2135314,5411,\"n:06315049-n | language | a system of words used to name things in a particular discipline\"],[0,11,2135746,5412,\"n:06315566-n | spoken word | a word that is spoken aloud\"],[0,11,2136092,5413,\"n:06317470-n | formative | minimal language unit that has a syntactic (or morphological) function\"],[0,