5831-n | headline | the heading or caption of a newspaper article\"],[0,11,2150649,5446,\"n:06357363-n | rubric | a heading that names a statute or legislative bill\"],[0,11,2151043,5447,\"n:06357831-n | title | a general or descriptive heading for a section of a written work\"],[0,11,2151434,5448,\"n:06360590-n | black and white | communication by means of written symbols (either printed or handwritten)\"],[0,11,2151920,5449,\"n:06360967-n | transcription | something written, especially copied from one medium to another, as a typewritten version of dictation\"],[0,11,2152427,5450,\"n:06361681-n | running hand | rapid handwriting in which letters are set down in full and are cursively connected within words without lifting the writing implement from the paper\"],[0,11,2153054,5451,\"n:06362325-n | italic | a style of handwriting with the letters slanting to the right\"],[0,11,2153442,5452,\"n:06362493-n | round hand | a clearly written style of longhand with large round curves\"],[0,11,2153839,5453,\"n:06362609-n | orthography | a method of representing the sounds of a language by written or printed symbols\"],[0,11,2154296,5454,\"n:06366714-n | secret code | a secret method of writing\"],[0,11,2154668,5455,\"n:06366866-n | international morse code | a telegraph code in which letters and numbers are represented by strings of dots and dashes (short and long signals)\"],[0,11,2155244,5456,\"n:06367112-n | zip code | a code of letters and digits added to a postal address to aid in the sorting of mail\"],[0,11,2155722,5457,\"n:06369392-n | machine code | a set of instructions coded so that the computer can use it directly without further translation\"],[0,11,2156220,5458,\"n:06371284-n | writing | letters or symbols that are written or imprinted on a surface to represent the sounds or words of a language\"],[0,11,2156704,5459,\"n:06374360-n | piece of writing | the work of a writer\"],[0,11,2157072,5460,\"n:06375185-n | writing | (usually plural) the collected work of a