,5725,\"n:06648469-n | details | true confidential information\"],[0,11,2267060,5726,\"n:06648638-n | dope | slang terms for inside information\"],[0,11,2267424,5727,\"n:06649049-n | book | a compilation of the known facts regarding something or someone\"],[0,11,2267836,5728,\"n:06652323-n | index | a number or ratio (a value on a scale of measurement) derived from a series of observed facts\"],[0,11,2268328,5729,\"n:06656171-n | evidence | an indication that makes something evident\"],[0,11,2268683,5730,\"n:06657156-n | fingerprint | a print made by an impression of the ridges in the skin of a finger\"],[0,11,2269099,5731,\"n:06659969-n | record | anything (such as a document or a phonograph record or a photograph) providing permanent evidence of or information about past events\"],[0,11,2269630,5732,\"n:06660359-n | proof | a formal series of statements showing that if one thing is true something else necessarily follows from it\"],[0,11,2270104,5733,\"n:06660791-n | demonstration | proof by a process of argument or a series of proposition proving an asserted conclusion\"],[0,11,2270581,5734,\"n:06660952-n | testimonial | something that serves as evidence\"],[0,11,2270941,5735,\"n:06662070-n | con | an argument opposed to a proposal\"],[0,11,2271263,5736,\"n:06662171-n | case | a statement of facts and reasons used to support an argument\"],[0,11,2271642,5737,\"n:06662815-n | confirmation | information that confirms or verifies\"],[0,11,2271999,5738,\"n:06662983-n | reenforcement | information that makes more forcible or convincing\"],[0,11,2272403,5739,\"n:06663176-n | certification | confirmation that some fact or statement is true through the use of documentary evidence\"],[0,11,2272901,5740,\"n:06663446-n | counsel | something that provides direction or advice as to a decision or course of action\"],[0,11,2273388,5741,\"n:06664322-n | confidential information | an indication of potential opportunity\"],[0,11,2273828,5742,\"n:06664987-n | prescript | prescribed guide for conduct or action\"],[0,11,2274188,5743,\"n:06668428-n | moral principle | the principle that conduct should be moral\"],[0,11,2274566,5744,\"n:06669153-n | policy | a line of argument rationalizing the course of action of a government\"],[0,11,2274978,5745,\"n:06669486-n | economic policy | a government policy for maintaining economic growth and tax revenues\"],[0,11,2275406,5746,\"n:06669854-n | new deal | the economic policy of F. D. Roosevelt\"],[0,11,2275753,5747,\"n:06670863-n | base | a lower limit\"],[0,11,2276048,5748,\"n:06673265-n | embargo | a government order imposing a trade barrier\"],[0,11,2276439,5749,\"n:06673687-n | foreign policy | a policy governing international relations\"],[0,11,2276812,5750,\"n:06674141-n | imperialism | a policy of extending your rule over foreign countries\"],[0,11,2277200,5751,\"n:06674492-n | noninterference | a foreign policy of staying out of other countries' disputes\"],[0,11,2277632,5752,\"n:06675457-n | neutralism | a policy of neutrality or nonalignment in international affairs\"],[0,11,2278036,5753,\"n:06675763-n | national trading policy | a government's policy controlling foreign trade\"],[0,11,2278463,5754,\"n:06676796-n | ordinance | an authoritative command\"],[0,11,2278800,5755,\"n:06677218-n | speed limit | regulation establishing the top speed permitted on a given road\"],[0,11,2279206,5756,\"n:06680062-n | code | a set of rules or principles or laws (especially written ones)\"],[0,11,2279606,5757,\"n:06681177-n | building code | set of standards established and enforced by local government for the structural safety of buildings\"],[0,11,2280094,5758,\"n:06681558-n | fire code | set of standards established and enforced by government for fire prevention and safety in case of fire as in fire escapes etc\"],[0,11,2280620,5759,\"n:06681938-n | health code | set of standards established and enforced by government for health requirements as in plumbing etc\"],[0,11,2281116,5760,\"n:06682129-n | highw