2311691,5837,\"n:06745868-n | protestation | a strong declaration of protest\"],[0,11,2312036,5838,\"n:06746225-n | threat | declaration of an intention or a determination to inflict harm on another\"],[0,11,2312447,5839,\"n:06746531-n | menace | a threat or the act of threatening\"],[0,11,2312781,5840,\"n:06746688-n | evidence | (law) all the means by which any alleged matter of fact whose truth is investigated at judicial trial is established or disproved\"],[0,11,2313310,5841,\"n:06747216-n | testimony | a solemn statement made under oath\"],[0,11,2313652,5842,\"n:06747572-n | corpus delicti | the body of evidence that constitute the offence\"],[0,11,2314037,5843,\"n:06747826-n | direct evidence | evidence (usually the testimony of a witness) directly related to the fact in dispute\"],[0,11,2314499,5844,\"n:06750143-n | contract | (contract bridge) the highest bid becomes the contract setting the number of tricks that the bidder must make\"],[0,11,2315004,5845,\"n:06750911-n | word | a brief statement\"],[0,11,2315297,5846,\"n:06751030-n | account | a statement that makes something comprehensible by describing the relevant structure or operation or circumstances etc.\"],[0,11,2315819,5847,\"n:06752425-n | value statement | a statement of the desirability of something\"],[0,11,2316199,5848,\"n:06752739-n | reason | an explanation of the cause of some phenomenon\"],[0,11,2316556,5849,\"n:06753097-n | cause | a justification for something existing or happening\"],[0,11,2316943,5850,\"n:06753339-n | defence | the justification for some act or belief\"],[0,11,2317319,5851,\"n:06753614-n | apologia | a formal written defense of something you believe in strongly\"],[0,11,2317724,5852,\"n:06753794-n | alibi | (law) a defense by an accused person purporting to show that they could not have committed the crime in question\"],[0,11,2318210,5853,\"n:06754000-n | alibi | a defense of some offensive behavior or some failure to keep a promise etc.\"],[0,11,2318681,5854,\"n:06755121-n | exposition | a systematic interpretation or explanation (usually written) of a specific topic\"],[0,11,2319133,5855,\"n:06755467-n | philosophizing | the exposition (often superficially) of a particular philosophy\"],[0,11,2319548,5856,\"n:06756201-n | answer | a statement that solves a problem or explains how to solve the problem\"],[0,11,2320004,5857,\"n:06756849-n | derivation | (historical linguistics) an explanation of the historical origins of a word or phrase\"],[0,11,2320482,5858,\"n:06757091-n | definition | a concise explanation of the meaning of a word or phrase or symbol\"],[0,11,2320891,5859,\"n:06759293-n | announcement | a public statement containing information about an event that has happened or is going to happen\"],[0,11,2321383,5860,\"n:06760197-n | handout | an announcement distributed to members of the press in order to supplement or replace an oral presentation\"],[0,11,2321893,5861,\"n:06761683-n | forecasting | a statement made about the future\"],[0,11,2322290,5862,\"n:06762595-n | forecast | a prediction about how something (as the weather) will develop\"],[0,11,2322699,5863,\"n:06762868-n | divination | a prediction uttered under divine inspiration\"],[0,11,2323079,5864,\"n:06763518-n | proposition | (logic) a statement that affirms or denies something and is either true or false\"],[0,11,2323519,5865,\"n:06765744-n | conclusion | the proposition arrived at by logical reasoning (such as the proposition that must follow from the major and minor premises of a syllogism)\"],[0,11,2324092,5866,\"n:06766013-n | posit | (logic) a proposition that is accepted as true in order to provide a basis for logical reasoning\"],[0,11,2324560,5867,\"n:06766514-n | assumption | a statement that is assumed to be true and from which a conclusion can be drawn\"],[0,11,2325019,5868,\"n:06768165-n | thesis | an unproved statement put forward as a premise in an argument\"],[0,11,2325406,5869,\"n:06768279-n | condition | an assumption on which rests the 