ach\"],[0,11,2333116,5888,\"n:06786777-n | peace treaty | a treaty to cease hostilities\"],[0,11,2333486,5889,\"n:06790003-n | caustic remark | witty language used to convey insults or scorn\"],[0,11,2333900,5890,\"n:06790633-n | backchat | light teasing repartee\"],[0,11,2334257,5891,\"n:06791616-n | laugh line | the point of a joke or humorous story\"],[0,11,2334665,5892,\"n:06793739-n | fun | verbal wit or mockery (often at another's expense but not to be taken seriously)\"],[0,11,2335101,5893,\"n:06794240-n | clowning | a comic incident or series of incidents\"],[0,11,2335488,5894,\"n:06794876-n | opinion | a message expressing a belief about something\"],[0,11,2335855,5895,\"n:06795537-n | conjecture | a message expressing an opinion based on incomplete evidence\"],[0,11,2336334,5896,\"n:06796455-n | estimate | a statement indicating the likely cost of some job\"],[0,11,2336705,5897,\"n:06796625-n | head | the subject matter at issue\"],[0,11,2337032,5898,\"n:06796860-n | problem | a question raised for consideration or solution\"],[0,11,2337395,5899,\"n:06797823-n | case | a problem requiring investigation\"],[0,11,2337720,5900,\"n:06799486-n | direction | a message describing how something is to be done\"],[0,11,2338106,5901,\"n:06801422-n | prescription | directions prescribed beforehand\"],[0,11,2338453,5902,\"n:06801937-n | stage direction | an instruction written as part of the script of a play\"],[0,11,2338853,5903,\"n:06802268-n | church doctrine | the written body of teachings of a religious group that are generally accepted by that group\"],[0,11,2339373,5904,\"n:06802899-n | dogma | a religious doctrine that is proclaimed as true without proof\"],[0,11,2339768,5905,\"n:06803702-n | incarnation | (Christianity) the Christian doctrine of the union of God and man in the person of Jesus Christ\"],[0,11,2340247,5906,\"n:06804229-n | sign | any nonverbal action or gesture that encodes a message\"],[0,11,2340655,5907,\"n:06805502-n | beam | a signal transmitted along a narrow path\"],[0,11,2341010,5908,\"n:06806088-n | sign | a public display of a message\"],[0,11,2341327,5909,\"n:06807231-n | guidepost | a post bearing a sign that gives directions or shows the way\"],[0,11,2341735,5910,\"n:06808400-n | brand | identification mark on skin, made by burning\"],[0,11,2342094,5911,\"n:06809500-n | birdcall | the characteristic sound produced by a bird\"],[0,11,2342482,5912,\"n:06810027-n | indicant | something that serves to indicate or suggest\"],[0,11,2342856,5913,\"n:06811045-n | symptom | anything that accompanies X and is regarded as an indication of X's existence\"],[0,11,2343278,5914,\"n:06811330-n | pointing out | indication by demonstration\"],[0,11,2343616,5915,\"n:06811416-n | manifestation | a manifest indication of the existence or presence or nature of some person or thing\"],[0,11,2344070,5916,\"n:06811608-n | mark | a visible indication made on a surface\"],[0,11,2344415,5917,\"n:06812755-n | line | a mark that is long relative to its width\"],[0,11,2344756,5918,\"n:06813202-n | dotted line | a line made up of dots or dashes\"],[0,11,2345103,5919,\"n:06813996-n | spectrum line | an isolated component of a spectrum formed by radiation at a uniform frequency\"],[0,11,2345547,5920,\"n:06814438-n | contour | a line drawn on a map connecting points of equal height\"],[0,11,2345942,5921,\"n:06814598-n | isometric line | a line connecting isometric points\"],[0,11,2346316,5922,\"n:06815429-n | forerunner | something that precedes and indicates the approach of something or someone\"],[0,11,2346797,5923,\"n:06815643-n | clue | a slight indication\"],[0,11,2347103,5924,\"n:06819327-n | symbol | an arbitrary sign (written or printed) that has acquired a conventional significance\"],[0,11,2347536,5925,\"n:06820056-n | number | a symbol used to represent a number\"],[0,11,2347883,5926,\"n:06820707-n | symbolism | a system of symbols and symbolic representations\"],[0,11,2348253,5927,\"n:06821351-n | notation | a techni