-n | impression | a symbol that is the result of printing or engraving\"],[0,11,2356119,5946,\"n:06873227-n | shake | a note that alternates rapidly with another note a semitone above it\"],[0,11,2356527,5947,\"n:06875109-n | staff line | any of the 5 horizontal marks comprising a staff\"],[0,11,2356902,5948,\"n:06876492-n | tenor clef | a clef that puts middle C on the fourth line of the staff\"],[0,11,2357296,5949,\"n:06876801-n | key | any of 24 major or minor diatonic scales that provide the tonal framework for a piece of music\"],[0,11,2357753,5950,\"n:06877775-n | bar | musical notation for a repeating pattern of musical beats\"],[0,11,2358135,5951,\"n:06878395-n | musical note | a notation representing the pitch and duration of a musical sound\"],[0,11,2358566,5952,\"n:06885726-n | tenor | the adult male singing voice above baritone\"],[0,11,2358931,5953,\"n:06887235-n | traffic light | a visual signal to control the flow of traffic at intersections\"],[0,11,2359378,5954,\"n:06887547-n | red light | the signal to stop\"],[0,11,2359690,5955,\"n:06887887-n | yellow light | the signal to proceed with caution\"],[0,11,2360043,5956,\"n:06889194-n | sign | a gesture that is part of a sign language\"],[0,11,2360384,5957,\"n:06889359-n | gesture | the use of movements (especially of the hands) to communicate familiar or prearranged signals\"],[0,11,2360850,5958,\"n:06891756-n | snarl | an angry vicious expression\"],[0,11,2361166,5959,\"n:06891853-n | straight face | a serious facial expression giving no evidence of interest or amusement\"],[0,11,2361594,5960,\"n:06892571-n | display | something intended to communicate a particular impression\"],[0,11,2361985,5961,\"n:06893299-n | expression | expression without words\"],[0,11,2362357,5962,\"n:06893583-n | exemplification | showing by example\"],[0,11,2362702,5963,\"n:06893714-n | allegory | a visible symbol representing an abstract idea\"],[0,11,2363086,5964,\"n:06895611-n | badge | an emblem (a small piece of plast