1-n | decline | change toward something smaller or lower\"],[0,11,3781660,9477,\"n:13480171-n | deepening | a process of becoming deeper and more profound\"],[0,11,3782026,9478,\"n:13482066-n | de iodination | the removal of iodine atoms from organic compounds\"],[0,11,3782412,9479,\"n:13482365-n | demand | the ability and desire to purchase goods and services\"],[0,11,3782783,9480,\"n:13483154-n | denial | (psychiatry) a defense mechanism that denies painful thoughts\"],[0,11,3783170,9481,\"n:13484693-n | desorption | changing from an adsorbed state on a surface to a gaseous or liquid state\"],[0,11,3783593,9482,\"n:13486023-n | development | a process in which something passes by degrees to a different stage (especially a more advanced or mature stage)\"],[0,11,3784111,9483,\"n:13486733-n | diffusion | (physics) the process in which there is movement of a substance from an area of high concentration of that substance to an area of lower concentration\"],[0,11,3784685,9484,\"n:13490877-n | drift | the gradual departure from an intended course due to external influences (as a ship or plane)\"],[0,11,3785134,9485,\"n:13493721-n | cataphoresis | the motion of charged particles in a colloid under the influence of an electric field\"],[0,11,3785643,9486,\"n:13494300-n | elimination | the bodily process of discharging waste matter\"],[0,11,3786070,9487,\"n:13495937-n | endothermic reaction | a chemical reaction accompanied by the absorption of heat\"],[0,11,3786493,9488,\"n:13496741-n | eating away | (geology) the mechanical process of wearing or grinding something down (as by particles washing over it), also figuratively\"],[0,11,3787072,9489,\"n:13499015-n | exothermic reaction | a chemical reaction accompanied by the evolution of heat\"],[0,11,3787490,9490,\"n:13503086-n | flare | a sudden burst of flame\"],[0,11,3787798,9491,\"n:13503390-n | flocculation | the process of flocculating\"],[0,11,3788135,9492,\"n:13504534-n | foreground processing | the execution of a pr