ibited in the United States by a constitutional amendment\"],[0,11,4287568,10734,\"n:15319850-n | incubation period | the period between infection and the appearance of symptoms of the disease\"],[0,11,4288014,10735,\"n:15320288-n | bloom | the period of greatest prosperity or productivity\"],[0,11,4288455,10736,\"n:15321021-n | running time | the length of time that a movie or tv show runs\"],[0,11,4288832,10737,\"n:80039599-n | working man | a male employee who performs manual or industrial labor\"],[0,11,4289249,10738,\"n:80847059-n | rifleman | a male soldier whose weapon is a rifle\"],[0,11,4289596,10739,\"n:81562204-n | medical man | a man who practices medicine\"],[0,11,4289932,10740,\"n:81566337-n | plainclothesman | a male detective who wears civilian clothes on duty\"],[0,11,4290326,10741,\"n:81664785-n | wise man | a male wise and trusted guide and advisor\"],[0,11,4290679,10742,\"n:82726249-n | infantryman | a man who fights on foot with small arms\"],[0,11,4291039,10743,\"n:82847232-n | patrolman | a male policeman who patrols a given region\"],[0,11,4291400,10744,\"n:83179919-n | chairman | the male officer who presides at the meetings of an organization\"],[0,11,4291799,10745,\"n:83297053-n | gunman | a male professional killer who uses a gun\"],[0,11,4292170,10746,\"n:84105775-n | lawman | a male officer of the law\"],[0,11,4292486,10747,\"n:84292585-n | marksman | a man skilled in shooting\"],[0,11,4292808,10748,\"n:84401307-n | maintenance man | a male skilled worker whose job is to repair things\"],[0,11,4293232,10749,\"n:84514344-n | cave man | a man who lives in a cave\"],[0,11,4293565,10750,\"n:85211648-n | childhood autism | formerly used for autism spectrum disorder with significant disability and symptoms starting in early childhood\"],[0,11,4294253,10751,\"n:86306106-n | craftsman | a male professional whose work is consistently of high quality\"],[0,11,4294666,10752,\"n:86343667-n | clergyman | a male member of the clergy and a spiritual leader of the Christian Church\"],[0,11,4295109,10753,\"n:86438461-n | second language | a language that a person has acquired in adolescence or later\"],[0,11,4295532,10754,\"n:86667468-n | altar girl | a girl serving as an acolyte\"],[0,11,4295867,10755,\"n:86712636-n | irish spelling | English orthography used in the UK, Ireland and most of the Commonwealth (characterized by ‘analyse’, ‘centre’ and ‘useable’)\"],[0,11,4296762,10756,\"n:86724964-n | highwayman | a holdup man who stops a vehicle and steals from it\"],[0,11,4297141,10757,\"n:87754171-n | man | a man who serves in the armed forces\"],[0,11,4297501,10758,\"n:88571022-n | playground ball | a large rubber ball used in various playground games including four square, kickball, and dodgeball\"],[0,11,4297993,10759,\"n:88722876-n | rifleman | a man skilled in the use of a rifle\"],[0,11,4298334,10760,\"n:88791161-n | busboy | a male restaurant attendant who sets tables and assists waiters and clears away dirty dishes\"],[0,11,4298783,10761,\"n:88810331-n | churchman | a male clergyman or other person in religious orders\"],[0,11,4299161,10762,\"n:88960729-n | hired man | a male hired laborer on a farm or ranch\"],[0,11,4299513,10763,\"n:89570581-n | feather | branching, hair-like structure that grows on the bodies of birds\"],[0,11,4299909,10764,\"n:92412100-n | carrot soup | soup made from carrots and other ingredients.\"],[0,11,4300281,10765,\"n:92412333-n | apple vodka | strong alcoholic beverage with apple flavour.\"],[0,11,4300671,10766,\"n:92412630-n | white currant | the white translucent edible berry of a group of cultivars of the red currant (Ribes rubrum).\"],[0,11,4301145,10767,\"n:92413959-n | cherry plum | an edible fruit of the small tree Prunus cerasifera.\"],[0,11,4301531,10768,\"n:92415441-n | chard soup | a soup made from chard.\"],[0,11,4301856,10769,\"n:92415702-n | linear metre | a meter in which the deflection of the pointer is proportional to the quantity measured.\"],[0,11,4302334,10770,\"n:92417573-n | eye colour | The pigmentation of the eye's iris.\"],[0,11,4302697,10771,\"n:92420754-n | gross weight | the total weight of a product and its packaging.\"],[0,11,4303078,10772,\"n:92424039-n | super heavyweight | A weight class division in combat sports, often the heaviest.\"],[0,11,4303517,10773,\"n:92425729-n | star atlas | (astronomy) a series of star maps for different times, for example, for each month\"],[0,11,4303961,10774,\"n:92427480-n | editorial file | a file that includes printouts ready for publishing.\"],[0,11,4304356,10775,\"n:92428867-n | foam glass | Cellular glass, also called foam glass or expanded glass is a light, opaque, cellular glass made by adding powdered carbon to crushed glass and firing the mixture.\"],[0,11,4304999,10776,\"n:92429524-n | optical isomer | one of two stereoisomers that are mirror images of each other that are non-superposable (not identical).\"],[0,11,4305498,10777,\"n:92429829-n | young blood | a younger member or members of a group considered as a revitalizing force, as in an organization.\"],[0,11,4305974,10778,\"n:92433086-n | quartz sand | sand that is mainly composed of quartz, used as the main raw material for commercial glass production.\"],[0,11,4306460,10779,\"n:92434568-n | pistachio green | A pale yellow-green colour, like that of the pistachio nut.\"],[0,11,4306872,10780,\"n:92435690-n | second molar | The seventh permanent tooth located in the upper and lower jaw on either side.\"],[0,11,4307313,10781,\"n:92437995-n | energy engineering | a broad field of engineering dealing with energy efficiency, energy services, facility management, plant engineering, environmental compliance and alternative energy technologies.\"],[0,11,4307974,10782,\"n:92439235-n | video art | a type of art which relies on moving pictures and comprises video and/or audio data.\"],[0,11,4308418,10783,\"n:92444179-n | pole weapon | a close combat weapon in which the main fighting part of the weapon is fitted to the end of a long shaft, typically of wood, thereby extending the user's effective range.\"],[0,11,4309052,10784,\"n:92446192-n | family film | a film genre that contains appropriate content for younger viewers but aims to appeal not only to children, but to a wide range of ages.\"],[0,11,4309623,10785,\"n:92446204-n | supply curve | in economics, graphic representation of the relationship between product price and quantity of product that a seller is willing and able to supply.\"],[0,11,4310202,10786,\"n:92447281-n | satellite triangulation | the branch of satellite geodesy in which geodetic problems are solved on the basis of positional (angular) observations of artificial earth satellites.\"],[0,11,4310823,10787,\"n:92448436-n | hammer axe | a weapon with a hammer on one side and an axe on the other.\"],[0,11,4311235,10788,\"n:92448504-n | water truck | a tank truck used to haul and disperse water.\"],[0,11,4311628,10789,\"n:92448703-n | film school | any educational institution dedicated to teaching aspects of filmmaking, including such subjects as film production, film theory, digital media production, and screenwriting.\"],[0,11,4312258,10790,\"n:92448847-n | keyhole neck | A neckline that forms a hole bellow the collarbones.\"],[0,11,4312669,10791,\"n:92449200-n | monitor speaker | One of the speakers on stage pointing towards the performers to help them hear themselves.\"],[0,11,4313161,10792,\"n:92449688-n | cosine curve | a curve whose equation in Cartesian coordinates is of the form y = a cos x.\"],[0,11,4313596,10793,\"n:92449693-n | tangent curve | a plane curve that is the graph of the equation y = tan x, where x is an angle.\"],[0,11,4314042,10794,\"n:92450165-n | laser interferometer | An interferometer which uses a laser as a light source\"],[0,11,4314460,10795,\"n:92450708-n | pocket calendar | A small calendar designed to fit in a pocket or a wallet\"],[0,11,4314905,10796,\"n:92450708-n | wallet calendar | A small calendar designed to fit in a pocket or a wallet\"],[0,11,4315350,10797,\"n:92450769-n | bath plug | A plug intended for washbasins, bath tubs and other similar water containers.\"],[0,11,4315825,10798,\"n:92450769-n | sink plug | A plug intended for washbasins, bath tubs and other similar water containers.\"],[0,11,4316300,10799,\"n:92450817-n | hunting whip | a whip carried by a mounted rider\"],[0,11,4316651,10800,\"n:92450958-n | red chalk | chalk of a reddish-brown colour that resembles dried blood\"],[0,11,4317056,10801,\"n:92459818-n | hydraulic motor | A hydraulic motor is a mechanical actuator that converts hydraulic pressure and flow into torque and angular displacement (rotation).\"],[0,11,4317616,10802,\"n:92459902-n | axial turbine | An axial flow turbine operates in the exactly reverse of an axial flow compressor,\"],[0,11,4318093,10803,\"n:92459943-n | cobalt machine | A machine used in the treatment of cancer with the use of gamma rays from cobalt-60 radioisotopes.\"],[0,11,4318580,10804,\"n:92460095-n | molecular pump | a vacuum pump that uses high speed jets of dense fluid or high speed rotating blades to knock gas molecules out of the chamber.\"],[0,11,4319125,10805,\"n:92460119-n | video file | a computer file that contains digitized video.\"],[0,11,4319496,10806,\"n:92460120-n | audio file | a computer file that contains digitized audio either in the Compact Disc (CDDA) format or in an MP3, AAC or other compressed format.\"],[0,11,4320039,10807,\"n:92460215-n | diesel hammer | A pile driving device consisting of a large two-stroke diesel engine.\"],[0,11,4320488,10808,\"n:92460638-n | web television | the genre of original television content produced for broadcast via the World Wide Web.\"],[0,11,4320964,10809,\"n:92460727-n | electronic music | a form of music consisting of sounds produced by oscillating electric currents either controlled from an instrument panel or keyboard or prerecorded on magnetic tape.\"],[0,11,4321593,10810,\"n:92460782-n | surf music | a genre of popular music associated with surf culture, particularly as found in Orange County and other areas of Southern California.\"],[0,11,4322138,10811,\"n:92460878-n | high vowel | a vowel sound made with your tongue near the top of your mouth.\"],[0,11,4322559,10812,\"n:92461160-n | cow brush | a stationary or rotating brush usually consisting of one horizontal and one vertical brush that cows use for scratching and grooming.\"],[0,11,4323118,10813,\"n:92461266-n | semaphore telegraph | a tower with pivoting shutters, also known as blades or paddles, used for conveying information by means of visual signals, read when the shutter is in a fixed position.\"],[0,11,4323784,10814,\"n:92461352-n | sawdust stove | a stove that is cheap and easy to make, burns either free or low-cost fuel.\"],[0,11,4324223,10815,\"n:92461435-n | optical telegraph | any telegraph that uses visual signals to convey a message, including the use of smoke signals, beacons or reflected light, which have existed since ancient times.\"],[0,11,4324849,10816,\"n:92461960-n | agglutinative language | a language in which words are made up of a linear sequence of distinct morphemes and each component of meaning is represented by its own morpheme.\"],[0,11,4325457,10817,\"n:92462261-n | complex preposition | a preposition that consists of a group of words that act as one unit.\"],[0,11,4325902,10818,\"n:92462411-n | fly press | a type of screw press in which the screw shaft is driven by a flywheel or a pair of fly weights at the ends of a bar.\"],[0,11,4326412,10819,\"n:92462705-n | electromagnetic transducer | a transducer that converts electromagnetic waves and magnetic fields to and from electrical signals.\"],[0,11,4326939,10820,\"n:92463288-n | long vowel | A vowel which is normally pronounced somewhat longer than other vowels (usually around 1½ to double length).\"],[0,11,4327436,10821,\"n:92463799-n | stay relay | a relay that maintains either contact position indefinitely without power applied to the coil.\"],